NAME
    readers - find static read references to an address

SYNOPSIS
    readers [<space>] <addr> [<scanstart> <scanlen>] [--json]

DESCRIPTION
    Scans CpuBus (or the named processor's code space when <space> is
    given) for instructions that statically read hex address <addr>. By
    default the scan covers <addr>'s own bank from $8000 to $FFFF; supply
    hex <scanstart> and <scanlen> to scan another range.

    Only statically encoded addressing modes on systems with a static
    disassembler are detected. When static disassembly is unavailable or
    when reads use indexed or indirect addressing, use 'watch add ...
    read' in watch(1) or 'bp read' in bp(1) for runtime read detection.

EXAMPLES
    readers 13c6
    readers WRAM 007E --json
    readers 13c6 808000 8000

EXIT STATUS
    0   Scan completed (or usage message printed).
    1   No target attached, invalid hex argument, or session service fault.

SEE ALSO
    writers(1), callers(1), disasm(1), bp(1), watch(1)
